In Vitest 4+, install the provider package with `npm i -D vitest @vitest/browser-webdriverio`. Then import its factory function and pass it as `test.browser.provider`:

```ts
// vitest.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config'
import { webdriverio } from '@vitest/browser-webdriverio'

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    browser: {
      enabled: true,
      provider: webdriverio(), // you can pass WebdriverIO options here, e.g. capabilities
      instances: [{ browser: 'chrome' }], // also 'firefox', 'edge', 'safari'
    },
  },
})
```

Run `npx vitest` (add `--browser.headless` for CI). Vitest 3 works differently: you install `@vitest/browser` and `webdriverio`, then set `provider: 'webdriverio'` as a string. I wrote this from memory and didn't check the current docs at vitest.dev/guide/browser.
